<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $117.4 mln March 10.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $117.4 mln March 10.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $117.4 million surplus on March 10 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MARCH 10</p>
<p>Exports: $247.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $151.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $177.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $156.8 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $117.4 million</p>
<p>MARCH DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.246 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.008 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.507 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.093 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $652 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485415))</p>
</text>
